# Cupertino dialogs + scroll

Cupertino alerts/sheets **do not scroll by themselves**. Long content is clipped.

## Choose the right surface

- `CupertinoActionSheet` — short action menus only (few buttons). **Not** for long field lists.
- `CupertinoAlertDialog` — info / confirm / long text. Prefer this for proxy geo info, disclaimers, view-URL.

## Long content must be height-capped

Compose `verticalScroll` only works when height is **bounded**. Without `heightIn(max=…)`, the column grows forever and nothing scrolls.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — ActionSheet + unbounded Column (clipped, no scroll)
CupertinoActionSheet(content = {
    Column { /* many InfoLines */ }
})

// ❌ BAD — scroll without max height
CupertinoText(text, Modifier.verticalScroll(rememberScrollState()))

// ✅ GOOD — cap height (~45–55% screen) then scroll
val maxH = (LocalConfiguration.current.screenHeightDp * 0.55f).dp
Column(
    Modifier
        .heightIn(max = maxH)
        .verticalScroll(rememberScrollState()),
) { /* … */ }
```

## Reuse project helper

For plain text bodies use `ScrollableDialogMessage` (`mtprotocompose/.../ScrollableDialogMessage.kt`).
For structured multi-line info (geo sheets) mirror `InfoBottomSheet`: `CupertinoAlertDialog` + `heightIn` + `verticalScroll` on the message `Column`.
